If the result text contains "my-image.png" and the media filename is "image.png", the bare filename match will replace a substring, potentially mangling the text. Consider word-boundary matching or anchoring to path separators when matching bare filenames:

```typescript
// Instead of text.indexOf(candidate), consider:
const regex = new RegExp(
  `(^|[\\s/])${escapeRegExp(candidate)}($|[\\s])`,
  "i"
);
```

This is a low-priority edge case since in practice tool output text typically contains the full path, not just a filename embedded in another word.

**`DefaultBlock` prop name shadowing**

