  if (renderContent) {   // shadows the old internal function name
    return renderContent(content);
  }
```

The prop `renderContent` previously named the internal function. Renaming the internal function to `renderBody` is correct, but consider whether `renderContent` is the best prop name — it could be confused with the old function. A name like `contentRenderer` or `renderBody` (matching the internal function) might be clearer:

```typescript
interface DefaultBlockProps {
  /** Optional custom renderer for the content body. */
  contentRenderer?: (content: string) => React.ReactNode;
}
```

